  "job_B1.5.6_20251001_193248": {
    "text": "Erat quidam regulus cuius filius infirmabatur Capharnaum & reliqua, Ure H\u00e6lend com hwilon to\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s sum underkyng on Capharnan burig, & his sune \u00f0a l\u00e6g seoc to for\u00f0fore.\n\u00d0a axode \u00fee underkyng embe \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes f\u00e6r, \u00fe\u00e6t he from Iudea londe com to Galileam, ferde \u00fea to\n\u00dea andswarde \u00fee H\u00e6lend \u00feus \u00f0am underkynge, Buton ge tacne iseon, nelle ge ilyf\u00e6n.\n\u00dee underkyng him andswarde eft, La, leof Drihten, fare to mine sune \u00e6r \u00fean \u00f0e he sw\u00e6lte.\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feus to, Fare \u00f0e nu on \u00feinne w\u00e6g; \u00fein sune leof\u00e6\u00f0.\n\u00d0a ilyfde \u00fee kyng \u00f0\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes sp\u00e6ce, & wende him hamweard, & hopode to \u00fean.\n\u00d0a comen \u00f0\u00e6s on maregen his men him togeanes & cydden him mid blisse \u00fe\u00e6t his sune leofede.\n\u00d0e f\u00e6der heom befran \u00fea mid fyrwetnysse son\u00e6, on hwylcere tide \u00fee sune gewurpte.\nHeo s\u00e6den him to andsware, Gyrst\u00e6nd\u00e6g he wurpte; swa ofer midne d\u00e6g, \u00fe\u00e6t hine forlet \u00feeo fefor.\n\u00dea oncneow \u00fee f\u00e6der \u00fe\u00e6t hine forlet \u00fee fefor on \u00feare ylc\u00e6 tide \u00fee \u00f0e H\u00e6lend him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Fare \u00fee nu\n& he \u00fea sylf ilyfde, & all his hired \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6t.\n\u00d0is godspel is nu sceortlice is\u00e6d on Englisc, & we wull\u00e6\u00f0 eow s\u00e6cg\u00e6n sum andgit \u00feerto of \u00feare\nUnderkyng is ihaten \u00fee under \u00feam casere rix\u00e6\u00f0; & on \u00feam time w\u00e6ron caseres on Rome swa \u00fe\u00e6t heo\n& heo kynelice rixoden fela hund geare; & heom mon feorran brohten of huwhilce londe \u00e6g\u00f0er ge lac\n\u00d0a w\u00e6ron \u00f0a underkyng\u00e6s \u00feam casere under\u00f0eode, to \u00f0am \u00f0e heo wolden, & heor\u00e6 wur\u00f0scipe w\u00e6s bi\n\u00d0\u00e6t cydde \u00fee casere \u00feam kynge Archelau \u00fe\u00e6s Herodis sune, \u00fee \u00fea childr\u00e6n acwalde.\nHe sette ut of kynestole & sende hine on wr\u00e6csi\u00f0e for his forwenednysse.\n& gesette for hine feower o\u00f0re kyng\u00e6s, \u00fea w\u00e6ren fi\u00f0erric\u00e6n, for \u00fean \u00f0e heor\u00e6 \u00e6lc h\u00e6fde feor\u00f0en d\u00e6l\nNu w\u00e6s \u00fees kyng \u00fee com to Criste underkyng ihaten on \u00fea ylcan wis\u00e6n, & he b\u00e6d his sune h\u00e6lu, swa\n\u00d0a andswarde \u00fee H\u00e6lend \u00feus \u00feam underkynge.\nButon ge tacn\u00e6 iseon, nylle ge ilef\u00e6n.\nN\u00e6s \u00fee kyng alles buton Cristes ileaf\u00e6n, \u00f0a \u00f0a he hine b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6lde his sune; ac he n\u00e6fde swa\nHe mihte h\u00e6len mid his h\u00e6se his sune, swa swa he \u00f0a dyde, \u00f0eah \u00f0e he ne si\u00f0ode ham to his huse mid\n\u00d0e kyng nyste \u00fea gyt \u00fe\u00e6t Crist mihte swa don & mid his worde hine h\u00e6len, & he for\u00fey bed hine \u00fe\u00e6t he\nGif he rihtlice ilyfde, he sceolde \u00f0onne witen \u00fe\u00e6t God sylf is \u00e6ghw\u00e6r, on \u00e6lcere stowe, \u00feurh his\nWen is \u00fe\u00e6t eower sum \u00feisses wundrige nu, hu \u00f0e Almihtig\u00e6 God \u00e6lcne mon ihere, beo \u00f0\u00e6r he beo, gif\nAc gesceaw\u00e6 \u00feas sunn\u00e6n hu heo scyn\u00e6\u00f0 \u00e6ghw\u00e6r & send hire leomen to alle londum endemes; & heo\nMycele swy\u00f0or m\u00e6g \u00fee Almihtig\u00e6 Wealdend his leomen senden to his ileaffullum monnum on\n\u00dee underkyng him andswarde, Efest la, leof Drihten, far to mine sun\u00e6 \u00e6r \u00fean \u00f0e he swelte.\nHer him tweonode eft for his andgitleaste.\nHe sceolde ilyfen \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee leof\u00e6 H\u00e6lend mihte his sune h\u00e6len swa swa he Lazarum dyde, \u00feeah \u00f0e he\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e Lazarus l\u00e6g on burigene feower niht fule \u00fea stincende; ac he for\u00f0 stop son\u00e6 \u00fea \u00f0e ure\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam kynge, Far \u00f0e nu on \u00f0ine w\u00e6g; \u00fein sune leof\u00e6\u00f0; & his sune wear\u00f0 swa from his\nSum hundredes aldor com to \u00feam H\u00e6lende hwilon on o\u00f0re stowe, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0us to him \u00fea, Eala, \u00f0u\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Ic cume me sylf to him & ic hine h\u00e6le.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee hundredes aldor, Ne am ic na wur\u00f0e, Drihten, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u swa don sceole, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u under mine\nIc sylf am nu an mon on anwealde iset, & ic habbe under me monig\u00e6 cniht\u00e6s on fare; & ic cw\u00e6\u00f0e to\n\u00d0a wundrode \u00fee H\u00e6lend his word\u00e6 & geleafen; & on ende cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Far \u00f0e nu hamweard, &\n& his cnap\u00e6 wear\u00f0 ih\u00e6led on \u00f0are ylcan tide.\n\u00d0e underkyng la\u00f0ode Crist to his huse ham; & he nolde swa \u00f0eah nateshwon mid him faren.\n& he wolde unla\u00f0od to \u00feam licgend\u00e6 cnap\u00e6 \u00fe\u00e6s hundredes aldres, swa swa ge ihyrdon nu for his\nWe ne cunnon wur\u00f0i\u00e6n witollice on monnum \u00fe\u00e6t heo Godes anlicnysse habb\u00e6\u00f0 on heom sylfum, ac \u00fea\nAc \u00fee H\u00e6lend nolde si\u00f0i\u00e6n mid \u00feam kynge, \u00f0eah \u00f0e he ibeden w\u00e6re; ac w\u00e6s gearu to farenne to \u00feam\n\u00d0a ilyfde \u00fee kyng \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes sp\u00e6ce, & wende, him hamweard, & hopode to \u00feam.\nOn \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes wordum he undernam geleafan; & s\u00e6 \u00f0e mid twynunge com to \u00f0am H\u00e6lende, \u00fee\n\u00d0a comen \u00f0\u00e6s on maregen his men him togeanes, & cyddon him mid blisse \u00fe\u00e6t his sune leofode.\n\u00dee f\u00e6der heom befran \u00f0a mid fyrwytnysse son\u00e6, on hwylcere tide \u00f0e sune wurpte.\nHeo s\u00e6den him to andsware, Gyrstend\u00e6g he wyrpte; swa ofer midne d\u00e6g \u00fe\u00e6t hine forlet \u00feeo feofer.\nOn \u00f0are seofo\u00f0en tide wear\u00f0 his sune ih\u00e6led, & \u00fe\u00e6t getel is halig \u00feurh \u00f0one Halg\u00e6 Gast on his\n\u00d0a oncneow \u00fee f\u00e6der \u00fe\u00e6t hine forlet \u00feeo feofer on \u00f0are ylcan tide \u00fee \u00f0e H\u00e6lend him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Fare\n\u00deeo Cristes boc us s\u00e6g\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Crist sylf bodede twegen dages on an on Samarian burig, & heo \u00f0a\nNu ilyfde \u00fees kyng on Crist mid his hirede \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6t an wundor \u00fee he wrohte on his sune; for\u00fean \u00f0e\n\u00d0a Iudeisce is\u00e6gen hu he wrohte tacn\u00e6 mycele & monig\u00e6 him sylfe tomiddes; ac swa \u00f0eah to feawe\n\u00d0a Iudeisce bocer\u00e6s bifrynnon hine hwilon, S\u00e6ge us, we bidd\u00e6\u00fe, on hw\u00e6s mihte \u00f0u wurc\u00e6st \u00feas\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend heom andswarde, S\u00e6cg\u00f0 me nu an \u00f0ing, w\u00e6s Iohannis fulluht of heofenum o\u00f0\u00f0e of\n\u00d0a smeadan \u00f0e bocer\u00e6s betwyx heom, \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0ende, Gif we him nu s\u00e6cg\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t his fulluht beo of\nGif we \u00feenne s\u00e6cg\u00e6\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t his fulluht is of monnum, \u00feenne wule al folc us oftorfi\u00e6n mid stanum, for\nHeo cw\u00e6den \u00fea to andsware, Nute we na to s\u00e6cgenne hwanon Iohannis fulluht beo; & \u00fee H\u00e6lend\n& heo let\u00e6n \u00fea swa.\n\u00dea bocer\u00e6s w\u00e6ron ablende on mode \u00fea \u00fea heo nolden s\u00e6cgen so\u00f0 be Iohanne, \u00f0onne heo w\u00e6l wiston\nFor \u00fean \u00f0e heo mihten icnaw\u00e6n, gif heo cy\u00f0en \u00e6nig god, \u00fe\u00e6t nan mon ne mihte makigen swylce\nSwa swa \u00fee sealmwurhte song hwilon bi Gode, Benedictus Dominus Deus Israelis, qui facit mirabilia\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e nan mon ne m\u00e6g nane mihte fremm\u00e6n, buton God wurce \u00fea wundr\u00e6 \u00f0urh \u00feone mon.\n\u00dee \u00f0e him sylf mak\u00e6\u00f0 mihte & wundr\u00e6 but\u00e6n \u00e6lcum men; \u00f0am is anweald & wuldor & wur\u00f0ment on\nAMEN.",
